<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is an automated conveyor system?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>An automated conveyor system uses PLCs, sensors, VFDs, and networked controls to transport, sort, accumulate, and process product without manual intervention. Automation levels range from simple start/stop motor control to fully integrated Industry 4.0 systems with real-time analytics and predictive maintenance.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">Warehouse automation vs. packaging line automation?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Warehouse automation focuses on case/tote transport and sortation at high throughput, measured in cartons or orders per hour. Packaging line automation focuses on product-level handling with tight machine synchronization, product protection, and frequent changeovers. Warehouse systems use <a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR</a> and <a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/">roller conveyors</a>. Packaging systems use belt, tabletop, and <a href="/conveyor-types/accumulation-conveyors/">accumulation conveyors</a>.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What PLC brands work for conveyor automation?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Allen-Bradley (Rockwell) is widely used in North American conveyor automation. Siemens is common in European installations. Beckhoff and B&amp;R serve high-speed and servo-intensive applications. The right choice usually follows the plant's existing PLC standard, mixing platforms increases maintenance costs and spare part complexity.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What sensors do automated conveyors use?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Photoelectric sensors (through-beam, retro-reflective, diffuse) detect product presence. Encoders measure belt speed and distance. Proximity sensors detect pallet and fixture positions. Barcode readers and RFID identify products for sorting and tracking. Vision cameras inspect labels, fill levels, and defects.</p>

</div>
